      en: "Bergen Museum (University Museum of Bergen) is a natural history and cultural history museum, founded in 1825. It belongs to the University of Bergen and has two main departments: natural history and cultural history. The natural history department displays minerals, fossils, and taxidermy, including a whale skeleton. The cultural history collection includes archaeological finds, medieval art, and traditional costumes. The museum is located in the city center, in the building of the former 'Bergens Museum'. Highlights include the 'Journey of the Birds' exhibition. The museum also runs the Bergen Botanical Garden. Around 100,000 people visit annually. Admission is free for students.",
